On 19 March 2003, the subject of gnomes and eggs was discussed in RGRN.
In *Ozma of Oz*, throwing an egg at a gnome (spelled "nome" in the book) 
causes instadeath for the unfortunate underground dweller so struck. I have 
thought for a long time that this would be a good addition to the game in a 
TDTTOE sort of way. Gnomes are such weak opponents that adding this feature 
would create no balance issues except for very low level characters, and it 
would add another use, albeit an obscure one, for eggs.

A second YANI is to explot the healing power of lichen. According to some 
foolish alternative medicine web site, "Usnea [aka Old Man's beard] can be 
applied directly to an open wound in emergency situations, it will serve as 
an antimicrobial compress to stop bleeding and prevent infection. Put this 
knowledge in your memory bank when you are in the woods, you never know when 
it may come in handy! Usnea extract has been shown to be effective against a 
wide spectrum of bacterial and fungal infections."

I therefore suggest that healers, and perhaps others, be given the option to 
(a)pply a lichen corpse to restore, say, d4 hitpoints. This would again 
present no balance issues beyond making the game slightly easier for 
low-level characters. It would also add a second use for the sadly 
underutilized lichen, a use that unspoiled players might reasonably deduce 
for themselves from their knowledge of RL.
I'm not a source diver, so I don't have any sense of whether adding (a)pply 
functionality to a foodstuff would be difficult.

